bluplay is a minimalistic, keyboard-driven terminal music player for
BluOS streamers (Bluesound, NAD, ...). It talks to the player over its
HTTP API on the LAN, lets you browse the player's local music library by
album or folder and manage the play queue. No streaming services, no
radio. It needs no libraries beyond libc and draws its own UI with
ANSI/VT100 escape sequences.

The player is found via mDNS, or set it in ~/.config/bluplay/config:
  host = 192.168.1.50

avahi-browse (from avahi) is used as an optional discovery fallback.
